    "case_id": "661",
    "case_summary": "A 36-year-old woman (gravida 2, para 2) presented with right lower pelvic pain. The patient had been previously diagnosed with presumed progressive uterine fibroids 6 months earlier and sought a second opinion.\n\nNo specific physical examination findings were reported in the case.\n\n- Imaging Studies:    1. Transabdominal sonography:       Image Title: Sonographic findings       Image Description: Hypoechoic mass measuring approximately 6.2 cm in diameter, with an irregular border over the right adnexa        2. Computed tomography:       Image Title: CT findings       Image Description: Moderately enhanced right adnexal tumor with an otherwise normal pelvic structure        3. Laparoscopic findings:       - Round and smooth surface mass arising from the isthmus of the right tube       - Fleshy mass bulging from the right cornual area        4. Pathological examination:       - Frozen section: Revealed a benign lesion       - Final pathology:         - Spindle cells and cords of epithelioid cells around numerous blood vessels         - Loose fibromyxoid stroma without mitotic atypia         - Immunohistochemistry: Positive for vimentin, desmin, smooth muscle actin, and estrogen and progesterone receptors         - Negative for cluster of differentiation 34 and pan-cytokeratin         - Well-demarcated border noted morphologically",
